    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on darwin1859-ch02-15: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.72";
    dc:description "Genus growth is testable with fossil data, but connecting it causally to present dominance and modified dominant descendants requires proxies. Different components are resolvable to different degrees.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Using fossil and dated phylogenetic time slices, test whether initially species-rich genera have higher subsequent net diversification and whether widespread abundant lineages leave more dominant descendants. Positive temporal effects support the prediction.";
